# GreenCart environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development, and add the same values in
# Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables for the live site.
#
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS COMMITTED AS A REAL VALUE. The secrets below must be set
# by whoever runs the deployment. `.env*` is git-ignored, and putting a real secret
# in a committed file gives it away permanently.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. The admin area — REQUIRED to see orders at all
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The password you type to open the admin panel. It accepts orders and edits the
# catalogue, so make it long and not a word you use elsewhere.
#
# Without it, the admin panel stays closed and every admin endpoint answers 503.
# That is deliberate: an open admin panel lets anyone read every order and change
# every price.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Optional. Signs the admin session cookie. If you leave it blank, a secret is
# derived from ADMIN_PASSWORD — which means changing the password signs everyone
# out, which is usually what you want. Set it only if you want to rotate sessions
# on a different schedule from the password.
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. The shared database — REQUIRED for orders to reach you
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without these, the shop still works, but everything a customer does is stored in
# their own browser and you never receive their order. The site says so plainly
# rather than pretending otherwise.
#
# Create a free Supabase project, then:
#   SUPABASE_SQL_URL         = https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/rest/v1/rpc/sql
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY = the "service_role" secret from Settings → API
#
# The service-role key bypasses row-level security. It is server-only: never put
# it in js/config.js, never prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_/VITE_, never paste it into
# a browser console.
SUPABASE_SQL_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. Card payments — leave blank until you have a Paystack account
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pay on delivery works without these. Card checkout stays visibly switched off
# until both are set.
#
# The secret key is used by api/ to talk to Paystack. Server-only.
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=

# The public key (pk_test_… or pk_live_…) goes in js/config.js, NOT here, because
# the browser needs it. Leave js/config.js's payments.publicKey empty while card
# payments are off.
#
# After setting a key, add this webhook in Paystack → Settings → API Keys & Webhooks:
#   https://your-domain/api/paystack-webhook
